-- A method used on a receiver that is already on a cycle is ONE
-- `infinite_type` at the use, the cycle poisoned, and no method looked up on
-- its head (checker-v2.md §9.5): `x` is
-- `Maybe x` once `[ x, Just x ]` is solved, before `x.foo ()` and `x == x`.
-- No `unknown_method` follows (`Maybe` has no `foo`): that is the cycle's
-- consequence. Known two-message case: with the method FIRST,
-- `( x.foo (), x == Just x )`,
-- the wanted is resolved on `Maybe a'` before the cycle closes, so its
-- `unknown_method` is honest then and both messages are given.
n x = ( [ x, Just x ], x.foo ⊤ )


m x = ( [ x, Just x ], x == x )
